1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 5)

3
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:05,879
Who are you looking for?

4
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,760
I'm here to see Pao Bei.

5
00:01:08,159 --> 00:01:08,959
Pao Bei?

6
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:09,560
Yeah.

7
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:10,920
Alright, just a moment.

8
00:01:11,879 --> 00:01:12,879
Okay.

9
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,760
Can I park this here?

10
00:01:22,079 --> 00:01:23,079
Sure.

11
00:01:29,359 --> 00:01:30,359
Excuse me,

12
00:01:30,519 --> 00:01:31,640
who are you looking for?

13
00:01:33,439 --> 00:01:36,519
Mingkun asked me to drop
off some things for Pao Bei.

14
00:01:37,599 --> 00:01:38,599
Follow me.

15
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,719
Oh, okay.

16
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:50,439
Let go of me!

17
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,680
What's your deal?

18
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:02,159
Fine, if you want to play,

19
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,439
can't you be a little gentler?

20
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:23,319
Scared now?

21
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,256
Still dare to mess with me?

22
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,599
I'm not scared of you.

23
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,000
Not one bit.

24
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,400
Call me Daddy.

25
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,960
Call me Daddy and I'll forgive you.

26
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,120
What's so funny?

27
00:02:47,759 --> 00:02:50,360
I'm laughing at how childish you are.

28
00:02:51,919 --> 00:02:53,120
What did you say?

29
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:58,400
Only little kids care about
making people call them Daddy.

30
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,080
Keep going.

31
00:03:10,159 --> 00:03:11,199
Why'd you stop?

32
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,000
Is that all you've got?

33
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,240
Have a seat for a moment.

34
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,999
Mr. Mingkun will be right with you.

35
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Oh, thanks.

36
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,240
Okay to step on this?

37
00:04:24,879 --> 00:04:25,879
Yes, go ahead.

38
00:04:26,199 --> 00:04:27,199
Okay.

39
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:38,600
Is this all of it?

40
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,600
Ah, yeah.

41
00:04:39,839 --> 00:04:41,160
That's everything Pao Bei has.

42
00:04:41,639 --> 00:04:42,758
Thanks for coming all this way.

43
00:04:42,759 --> 00:04:43,759
Please, have a seat.

44
00:04:44,279 --> 00:04:46,040
Peter, get Mr. A Pong a glass of water.

45
00:04:53,639 --> 00:04:54,639
Pao Bei?

46
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,160
Pao Bei!

47
00:04:56,639 --> 00:04:57,319
Pao Bei!

48
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,480
Wake up!

49
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,720
Pao Bei!

50
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,680
Mingkun!

51
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:10,719
Excuse me for a moment.

52
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,720
I'll be right back.

53
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,920
Sure.

54
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:13,959
Go ahead.

55
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:22,279
Mingkun!

56
00:05:22,319 --> 00:05:23,319
Mingkun!

57
00:05:23,959 --> 00:05:25,959
Wake up!

58
00:05:36,959 --> 00:05:38,199
You freaking tricked me!

59
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,240
Get back here!

60
00:06:15,519 --> 00:06:16,560
Help!

61
00:06:17,079 --> 00:06:17,920
Somebody help!

62
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,839
Help me!

63
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,000
That's Pao Bei's voice!

64
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,239
Did you guys hear that?

65
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,079
Help!

66
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,960
It's none of your business.
Back to your posts.

67
00:06:27,279 --> 00:06:28,279
Get over here!

68
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:31,360
Mingkun, save me!

69
00:06:32,079 --> 00:06:33,079
He's trying to kill me!

70
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,720
Who's trying to kill you?

71
00:06:35,759 --> 00:06:37,039
A Pong? What are you doing here?

72
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:38,439
Young Master!

73
00:06:38,519 --> 00:06:39,639
I knew it was you again!

74
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,759
Today—.

75
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,320
Today, I'm gonna do the world a favor!

76
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:43,319
Young Master!

77
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:44,319
A Pong, calm down!

78
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:45,680
We were just messing around!

79
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,240
Let go!

80
00:06:49,879 --> 00:06:51,198
He wasn't trying to kill me.

81
00:06:51,199 --> 00:06:52,160
Seriously, believe me!

82
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:53,160
Swear to it, then!

83
00:06:53,759 --> 00:06:54,759
I swear to God!

84
00:06:55,199 --> 00:06:56,519
If I'm lying,

85
00:06:56,759 --> 00:06:58,039
may the heavens punish me

86
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,040
by making me marry him!

87
00:06:59,079 --> 00:07:00,079
Happy now?

88
00:07:05,639 --> 00:07:06,919
You're coming with me right now.

89
00:07:07,759 --> 00:07:08,759
Young Master!

90
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:11,800
Young Master!

91
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,160
Stop fighting!

92
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:16,959
Stop it!

93
00:07:17,279 --> 00:07:18,319
Everybody, stop right now!

94
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,160
Pao Bei?

95
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:55,480
What happened to you?

96
00:07:55,481 --> 00:07:56,519
Why are you soaking wet?

97
00:07:56,759 --> 00:07:58,639
Go change your clothes
before you catch a cold.

98
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,920
I'm fine.

99
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,696
Just did some chores earlier.

100
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,720
Oh.

101
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:07,879
What's going on?

102
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,240
Why is he here too?

103
00:08:09,439 --> 00:08:10,920
And dressed like that?

104
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:12,959
A Pong?

105
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
What brings you here?

106
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,040
Oh.

107
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,920
Let's go.

108
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,920
What a wasted trip.

109
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,520
Ended up in a total mess for nothing.

110
00:08:23,959 --> 00:08:24,680
What do you mean?

111
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,680
Where are we going?

112
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:27,119
Your boss said

113
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,120
you're free to go.

114
00:08:28,519 --> 00:08:30,359
Guess that fight wasn't
for nothing after all.

115
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,079
Did he really say I could leave?

116
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:33,519
Mingkun?

117
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,080
Yes.

118
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,000
Fine, if you want to play,

119
00:09:26,001 --> 00:09:27,201
can't you be a little gentler?

120
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,600
Scared now?

121
00:09:31,519 --> 00:09:32,599
Still dare to mess with me?

122
00:09:32,799 --> 00:09:33,960
I'm not scared of you.

123
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,360
Not one bit.

124
00:09:35,679 --> 00:09:36,480
Call me Daddy.

125
00:09:36,481 --> 00:09:37,881
Call me Daddy and I'll forgive you.

126
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,080
Is he really not afraid?

127
00:09:51,519 --> 00:09:53,599
It's the first time I've
seen that look in his eyes.

128
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,720
And as for me,

129
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:57,399
why did it suddenly remind
me of myself as a kid?

130
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:12,840
Young Master.

131
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,480
What is it?

132
00:10:14,639 --> 00:10:16,639
Should I send Mr. Milan to your room?

133
00:10:24,399 --> 00:10:25,399
What do you mean?

134
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,559
Why would you call him here?

135
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:27,760
Isn't this your usual routine?

136
00:10:30,759 --> 00:10:32,558
He's currently terminating
his contract with his old agency.

137
00:10:32,559 --> 00:10:33,879
He's an artist I'm about to sign.

138
00:10:34,639 --> 00:10:36,399
I don't sleep with my own staff.

139
00:10:37,279 --> 00:10:38,480
Right, understood.

140
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,240
Didn't he say anything?

141
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,480
By "he," you mean...

142
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,039
Do I need to book you a brain scan?

143
00:10:47,159 --> 00:10:48,759
If you mean the "he" I'm thinking of,

144
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:50,240
he didn't say a word.

145
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,640
Didn't beg me to stay, either.

146
00:10:51,919 --> 00:10:54,080
In fact, he looked pretty happy about it.

147
00:10:54,159 --> 00:10:55,839
You've been talking a bit too much lately.

148
00:10:56,679 --> 00:10:58,240
I wasn't finished yet, Young Master.

149
00:10:58,559 --> 00:10:59,559
Spill it.

150
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,518
Well, Mr. Milan just asked

151
00:11:02,519 --> 00:11:03,678
about the personal assistant he needs.

152
00:11:03,679 --> 00:11:05,559
Will we provide one, or
should he hire his own?

153
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,240
You decide.

154
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,360
Shall I get you some painkillers?

155
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,360
No need.

156
00:12:00,159 --> 00:12:02,279
Trying to get rid of me
so I don't ruin your fun?

157
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:04,519
Expecting me to just walk away like this?

158
00:12:05,639 --> 00:12:06,720
No way in hell.

159
00:12:07,679 --> 00:12:08,960
Even if I leave,

160
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:12,080
I'm getting some dirt on you first.

161
00:12:36,759 --> 00:12:38,879
Wait, did he go to Milan's room to...

162
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:47,639
No, forget it.

163
00:12:48,279 --> 00:12:49,919
He's always been that kind of guy anyway.

164
00:12:50,039 --> 00:12:51,359
Never sincere with anyone.

165
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,759
Just a rich playboy.

166
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,360
My top priority right now

167
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:58,360
is to get dirt on him

168
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,039
and gather evidence.

169
00:13:07,159 --> 00:13:08,799
Why are the key and the doll both gone?

170
00:13:12,519 --> 00:13:13,840
Don't tell me he found out.

171
00:13:15,639 --> 00:13:16,919
Or maybe...

172
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:20,559
he hated the new clothes
I made and threw it away?

173
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,480
What the heck?

174
00:13:22,679 --> 00:13:23,879
What kind of person does that?

175
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,840
Listen carefully.

176
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,159
Only the Young Master
is allowed in this room.

177
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,879
Anyone else who enters without permission

178
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:39,840
will face severe punishment.

179
00:14:16,759 --> 00:14:17,759
Didn't you leave?

180
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,440
Who said I left?

181
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,200
I said I'd wait—

182
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,576
wait for the rain to stop before leaving.

183
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:26,799
Then what about your friend?

184
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,360
He didn't leave.

185
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,959
Probably fell asleep in my room.

186
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,960
Then why did you show
up at the door of that room?

187
00:14:33,919 --> 00:14:34,679
I...

188
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:37,278
I was just looking around to see

189
00:14:37,279 --> 00:14:38,559
if there was an empty room.

190
00:14:38,759 --> 00:14:40,319
Couldn't you just ask Mingkun for that?

191
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,320
You think I'm like you,

192
00:14:42,559 --> 00:14:44,079
bossing Mingkun around for everything?

193
00:14:52,159 --> 00:14:53,159
Come here.

194
00:14:55,159 --> 00:14:56,120
What now?

195
00:14:56,121 --> 00:14:57,281
Aren't you tired of standing?

196
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,480
I'm fine sitting right here.

197
00:15:36,919 --> 00:15:38,039
What are you doing now?

198
00:15:56,799 --> 00:15:57,799
Did you...

199
00:15:58,279 --> 00:15:59,279
make this?

200
00:16:00,279 --> 00:16:01,600
So you didn't throw it away.

201
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,360
Throw it away?

202
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,039
Are you crazy?

203
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,879
This thing means the world to me.

204
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:09,560
Why would I ever throw it out?

205
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,559
Who's talking about your doll?

206
00:16:12,039 --> 00:16:13,039
I thought...

207
00:16:14,679 --> 00:16:15,679
You thought what?

208
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:19,919
Nothing.

209
00:16:22,919 --> 00:16:23,919
Spit it out.

210
00:16:24,159 --> 00:16:25,159
Don't make me force you.

211
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,919
I just thought...

212
00:16:33,799 --> 00:16:35,279
I thought you didn't like the outfit.

213
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,520
It's not that I don't like it.

214
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,440
It's just...

215
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:48,960
this is its first time wearing new clothes.

216
00:16:49,559 --> 00:16:50,879
It doesn't matter if I like it.

217
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,279
What matters is that it likes it.

218
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:00,919
Does it like it, then?

219
00:17:03,279 --> 00:17:04,400
Are you out of your mind?

220
00:17:04,839 --> 00:17:06,519
Making me ask a doll that can't even talk?

221
00:17:07,519 --> 00:17:09,240
A doll having its own preferences?

222
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,119
Doesn't that sound even crazier?

223
00:17:16,319 --> 00:17:17,400
Yeah.

224
00:17:17,559 --> 00:17:18,559
You're right.

225
00:17:19,519 --> 00:17:20,640
I am crazy.

226
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:23,240
But...

227
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:26,039
you're pretty messed up yourself.

228
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,559
Are you going to sleep?

229
00:18:15,039 --> 00:18:16,039
Yeah.

230
00:18:16,279 --> 00:18:17,279
I'm sleepy.

231
00:19:23,839 --> 00:19:24,839
What's wrong?

232
00:19:25,119 --> 00:19:26,960
Weren't you trying to strangle me earlier?

233
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:28,896
What kind of game are you playing now?

234
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,280
Didn't you say you weren't scared?

235
00:19:30,359 --> 00:19:31,720
I'm not scared.

236
00:19:32,079 --> 00:19:33,679
But for the sake of my brother and sister,

237
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,798
I'd like to live a few more years.

238
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:35,720
Unlike you.

239
00:19:35,721 --> 00:19:37,240
You only have a brother and sister.

240
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,280
I'm responsible for an
entire corporation of people.

241
00:19:40,519 --> 00:19:42,519
I don't like people with a bad temper.

242
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,758
Have you ever stopped
to think why I got mad?

243
00:19:45,759 --> 00:19:46,759
I...

244
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,758
It's not like I lied to you on purpose.

245
00:19:49,759 --> 00:19:51,400
I thought I could fix it.

246
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,880
It was already broken to begin with.

247
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:55,960
Already broken?

248
00:19:55,961 --> 00:19:57,361
Then why did you blow up like that?

249
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:04,278
The problem is you glued it so tightly

250
00:20:04,279 --> 00:20:05,719
it took me forever to get it apart,

251
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,720
you know that?

252
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,680
You're lucky I didn't make you pay for it,

253
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,439
and you're the one giving me an attitude?

254
00:20:21,519 --> 00:20:22,519
Turn around.

255
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,200
Turn around!

256
00:20:31,559 --> 00:20:33,000
Gonna use force again, huh?

257
00:20:38,559 --> 00:20:40,079
Are you going to admit you were wrong?

258
00:20:42,839 --> 00:20:43,880
Fine, I was wrong.

259
00:20:44,599 --> 00:20:46,440
I never should've messed with you that day.

260
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,039
Since you already did,

261
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,160
just accept your fate.

262
00:20:56,359 --> 00:20:57,440
Ow!

263
00:21:03,519 --> 00:21:04,839
That really hurts!

264
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,038
Let go!

265
00:21:07,039 --> 00:21:08,039
It hurts!

266
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:10,335
If you can't even handle
this little bit of pain,

267
00:21:10,359 --> 00:21:11,919
what are you going to do in the future?

268
00:21:13,759 --> 00:21:14,880
What do you mean?

269
00:21:15,039 --> 00:21:16,399
What do you mean, "in the future"?

270
00:21:19,079 --> 00:21:20,079
Hey!

271
00:21:20,559 --> 00:21:21,279
I'm asking you a question!

272
00:21:21,279 --> 00:21:22,279
What do you mean by that?

273
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:24,200
You'll find out eventually.

274
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,160
Go to sleep.

275
00:22:16,119 --> 00:22:17,559
Putting it out with that much left?

276
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:21,799
Didn't someone say

277
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,319
smoking is bad for my throat?

278
00:22:25,799 --> 00:22:27,960
Since when do you care about your throat?

279
00:22:33,079 --> 00:22:35,960
Actually, I've always wanted to know

280
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:39,880
why you came to Tailan
without saying a word back then,

281
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:42,240
and deliberately cut
off all contact with me—

282
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,160
with us.

283
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:50,279
Everyone has their own path to walk.

284
00:22:51,039 --> 00:22:52,079
Meeting,

285
00:22:52,599 --> 00:22:53,599
parting,

286
00:22:53,839 --> 00:22:54,920
reuniting—

287
00:22:56,039 --> 00:22:57,519
it's all just a normal part of life.

288
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:00,680
The most important thing
is to live in the present.

289
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:10,920
Then do you know

290
00:23:12,079 --> 00:23:14,160
why I insisted on coming to Tailan to work?

291
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,599
To make money, obviously.

292
00:23:17,799 --> 00:23:18,799
What else could it be?

293
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:38,118
I didn't expect you to accept the offer

294
00:23:38,119 --> 00:23:40,038
from Yingyu Group so readily, Mr. Milan.

295
00:23:40,039 --> 00:23:42,559
Coming to work in Tailan is
something I've been fixated on.

296
00:23:44,079 --> 00:23:45,079
Oh?

297
00:23:45,119 --> 00:23:46,119
Why is that?

298
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:48,400
I'm looking for someone.

299
00:23:49,359 --> 00:23:50,959
Someone I've known for a very long time.

300
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,079
All I know is that he
came to Tailan to work,

301
00:23:55,519 --> 00:23:56,519
so I want to find him.

302
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:05,920
Why aren't you asleep yet?

303
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:07,440
What about you?

304
00:24:09,359 --> 00:24:10,480
I'm waiting for Pao Bei.

305
00:24:12,559 --> 00:24:13,879
I doubt he's coming back tonight.

306
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:17,400
Did he tell you that?

307
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:23,240
How about we make a bet?

308
00:24:24,759 --> 00:24:25,759
Bet on what?

309
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:29,000
Let me think.

310
00:24:31,079 --> 00:24:32,319
If I win,

311
00:24:32,599 --> 00:24:33,959
how about you become my assistant?

312
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:35,640
No way.

313
00:24:36,119 --> 00:24:38,199
Are you scared to bet, or
scared to be my assistant?

314
00:24:39,119 --> 00:24:39,720
Hey,

315
00:24:40,079 --> 00:24:41,798
I have a perfectly good
job at the restaurant.

316
00:24:41,799 --> 00:24:42,999
Why would I be your assistant?

317
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:45,599
Besides, aren't you signing with that jerk?

318
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:47,360
There's no way I'm working under him.

319
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:49,200
He won't be the one bossing you around.

320
00:24:49,839 --> 00:24:51,319
You just need to help me out.

321
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:53,240
He'd still be my boss on paper.

322
00:24:57,559 --> 00:24:59,200
So are you taking the bet or not?

323
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Well...

324
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:05,720
Forget it, coward.

325
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:07,519
I knew you wouldn't dare.

326
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:21,239
These are the leftover lottery
tickets I couldn't sell earlier.

327
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:22,680
If there's a winning ticket in here,

328
00:25:23,039 --> 00:25:24,039
I'll be your assistant.

329
00:25:24,559 --> 00:25:25,559
How about that?

330
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,680
Do you dare take that bet?

331
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,920
The odds of winning are way too low!

332
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:34,440
So, do you dare or not?

333
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,920
Deal.

334
00:25:40,119 --> 00:25:41,599
And if none of them win,

335
00:25:41,799 --> 00:25:43,400
I'll buy out all your tickets tomorrow.

336
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,216
You really have no head
for business, do you?

337
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,240
I was just kidding.

338
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,000
I'm not kidding.

339
00:25:51,359 --> 00:25:52,359
I'll take the bet.

340
00:25:57,319 --> 00:25:58,799
I believe in miracles.

341
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:03,000
Fine.

342
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:04,160
As long as you're in.

343
00:26:04,599 --> 00:26:05,759
Just don't cry when you lose.

344
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:27,839
Boss!

345
00:26:27,839 --> 00:26:28,839
We're back!

346
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:31,559
Boss, we're back!

347
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:34,080
Pace yourself with the drinks!

348
00:26:37,839 --> 00:26:38,839
Boss!

349
00:26:41,359 --> 00:26:42,359
Boss, we're heading out.

350
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:43,400
Hope you enjoyed the food!

351
00:26:44,039 --> 00:26:44,680
Take care!

352
00:26:44,681 --> 00:26:45,798
Come again next time!

353
00:26:45,799 --> 00:26:46,799
Sure!

354
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:48,240
Get home safe!

355
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:51,400
Boss, why aren't you
welcoming the two of us back?

356
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:53,880
If you're here as customers,

357
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,079
of course you're welcome.

358
00:26:56,039 --> 00:26:56,759
Wait,

359
00:26:56,760 --> 00:26:58,640
Boss, we've only been gone a few days.

360
00:26:58,799 --> 00:27:00,439
How can you act like you don't know us?

361
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:01,798
How could I forget?

362
00:27:01,799 --> 00:27:03,735
A Pong and Pao Bei, the guys
who started a brawl in my restaurant

363
00:27:03,759 --> 00:27:07,200
and smashed up the place.

364
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:11,000
Boss, what happened last
time was definitely my fault.

365
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,480
I promise you it'll never happen again.

366
00:27:13,759 --> 00:27:14,799
I'm really sorry about it.

367
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:15,720
Please forgive me.

368
00:27:15,721 --> 00:27:16,960
Save your apologies.

369
00:27:17,359 --> 00:27:20,119
Boss P'Eng already
paid for all the damages.

370
00:27:21,119 --> 00:27:22,839
Please let bygones be bygones.

371
00:27:23,400 --> 00:27:25,720
The two of us will definitely
work even harder from now on

372
00:27:25,799 --> 00:27:26,999
and cook even better
dishes for the customers.

373
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Boss, more beer!

374
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:29,240
Coming right up!

375
00:27:31,960 --> 00:27:32,960
What do we do?

376
00:27:36,079 --> 00:27:37,079
Enjoy!

377
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:39,000
Let's just go get changed first.

378
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:39,640
Come on.

379
00:27:39,799 --> 00:27:41,319
Hey, where do you think you're going?

380
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:44,839
To serve the customers!

381
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:47,558
I already told you, don't bother.

382
00:27:47,559 --> 00:27:49,078
I can't afford to keep you two on anymore.

383
00:27:49,079 --> 00:27:50,239
If you're not here to eat,

384
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:51,240
please leave.

385
00:27:51,799 --> 00:27:52,319
Wait,

386
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,039
Boss!

387
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,879
Didn't we just promise
there wouldn't be a next time?

388
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:56,319
Even so, I can't hire you back.

389
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:59,078
I can't afford to offend a
massive corporation again.

390
00:27:59,079 --> 00:28:00,439
I'm just running a small business here.

391
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:01,799
I don't have the guts for that.

392
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:03,640
Boss,

393
00:28:03,799 --> 00:28:04,879
I'm begging you.

394
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:06,479
Just give us one more chance.

395
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,159
I guarantee those guys will
never come back here again.

396
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:09,240
Please, Boss.

397
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:10,480
Boss, seriously.

398
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,279
Boss,

399
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:12,518
just give us one more shot.

400
00:28:12,519 --> 00:28:14,295
Their people already
made it very clear to me.

401
00:28:14,319 --> 00:28:17,199
They offered free promotion
and a partnership for my restaurant,

402
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,519
on one condition—

403
00:28:18,759 --> 00:28:20,400
I can't employ the two of you anymore.

404
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:21,920
I'm a businessman, after all.

405
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:23,759
A deal is a deal.

406
00:28:24,759 --> 00:28:25,839
Just go home.

407
00:28:28,279 --> 00:28:29,480
That damned devil!

408
00:28:29,799 --> 00:28:31,440
How dare he mess with our livelihood!

409
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:34,519
Shake it off.

410
00:28:34,839 --> 00:28:35,960
We're good cooks.

411
00:28:36,279 --> 00:28:37,720
We'll definitely find another job.

412
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:44,039
The harder life gets,

413
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:45,400
the harder I'll fight!

414
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:46,880
Hang in there, Pao Bei!

415
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:48,839
I can't let him look down on me!

416
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:27,160
What's wrong?

417
00:29:31,359 --> 00:29:32,719
Should I call him over?

418
00:29:32,720 --> 00:29:33,720
Why would I call him?

419
00:29:34,119 --> 00:29:35,639
Wasn't he the one who wanted to leave?

420
00:29:36,079 --> 00:29:36,839
If he wants to go, let him go!

421
00:29:36,840 --> 00:29:37,920
Nobody asked him to stay!

422
00:29:38,039 --> 00:29:39,679
Besides, he owes me
money in the first place!

423
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:40,758
Doesn't he have to pay off his debt?

424
00:29:40,759 --> 00:29:41,798
What the hell is his problem?

425
00:29:41,799 --> 00:29:43,880
And what do you mean
by asking to call him over?

426
00:29:45,039 --> 00:29:46,199
What I meant was,

427
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:48,320
should I call Master Chen
over to give you a massage?

428
00:29:48,359 --> 00:29:50,680
Your shoulders look a little stiff.

429
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,279
Why are you meddling so much?

430
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:58,160
Do I look that fragile to you?

431
00:29:58,559 --> 00:29:59,880
Right, my mistake.

432
00:30:00,079 --> 00:30:01,160
Please get some rest.

433
00:30:02,119 --> 00:30:03,119
Oh, by the way,

434
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,758
tomorrow I'm accompanying Mr. Milan

435
00:30:04,759 --> 00:30:06,440
to that event at the amusement park.

436
00:30:06,880 --> 00:30:09,240
Also, we need to find him an
assistant as soon as possible.

437
00:30:09,319 --> 00:30:10,319
Got it.

438
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:20,255
Are you sure you don't
want me to call him over?

439
00:30:20,279 --> 00:30:21,679
I already told you not to call him!

440
00:30:22,119 --> 00:30:23,119
Stop nagging!

441
00:30:25,839 --> 00:30:27,880
This time, I actually meant "him."

442
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:31,640
Why would I look for him?

443
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:33,400
I don't care if he comes back or not!

444
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:34,760
Whoever goes looking for him

445
00:30:35,319 --> 00:30:36,319
is a dog!

446
00:30:47,319 --> 00:30:49,359
Do you know what time it
is? Why isn't he home yet?

447
00:30:51,079 --> 00:30:52,079
Now that he's free,

448
00:30:52,119 --> 00:30:53,639
he's probably out partying like crazy.

449
00:31:10,599 --> 00:31:11,599
Hello?

450
00:31:11,839 --> 00:31:13,959
Yes, I'm the one who came
in for the interview today.

451
00:31:15,599 --> 00:31:16,640
Okay, I understand.

452
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:18,720
If you ever need a chef in the future,

453
00:31:18,799 --> 00:31:20,359
please feel free to contact me anytime.

454
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:35,759
What are you doing here?

455
00:31:37,279 --> 00:31:38,279
I...

456
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:41,599
I came to see if you ran
away like your mom did.

457
00:31:42,559 --> 00:31:43,959
I'm not going to run away.

458
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:44,720
Don't worry.

459
00:31:44,721 --> 00:31:46,681
I'll still go work at the
nursery during the day.

460
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:48,680
I'll do everything I'm supposed to do.

461
00:31:48,759 --> 00:31:50,495
Not like I have a choice, since
you cut off all my other options.

462
00:31:50,519 --> 00:31:51,559
Cut off your options?

463
00:31:52,279 --> 00:31:53,359
What are you talking about?

464
00:31:53,519 --> 00:31:55,119
Drop the act, Boss P'Eng.

465
00:31:55,559 --> 00:31:56,919
Weren't you the one who told my boss

466
00:31:56,920 --> 00:31:58,640
to fire A Pong and me?

467
00:31:58,680 --> 00:31:59,758
Thanks to you,

468
00:31:59,759 --> 00:32:01,480
we're both unemployed now. Happy?

469
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:03,696
When did I ever give your
boss an order like that?

470
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:04,759
You're the boss!

471
00:32:05,119 --> 00:32:06,976
He specifically said it was
someone from Yingyu Group.

472
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,000
If you didn't give the order,

473
00:32:08,001 --> 00:32:09,200
who else would dare do that?

474
00:32:10,039 --> 00:32:11,456
Don't accuse me of things I didn't do!

475
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:12,839
I never gave any order like that.

476
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,039
If you don't believe me,

477
00:32:14,759 --> 00:32:15,799
go ask Mingkun.

478
00:32:16,319 --> 00:32:17,319
Mingkun?

479
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:18,919
Doesn't Mingkun work for you anyway?

480
00:32:18,920 --> 00:32:20,480
What's the point of asking him?

481
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:21,920
Forget it.

482
00:32:22,279 --> 00:32:24,359
I refuse to believe I can't
find a single restaurant

483
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:25,799
that needs a great chef like me.

484
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:33,240
Is there anything else, Boss P'Eng?

485
00:32:33,759 --> 00:32:35,319
You didn't bring your goons this time,

486
00:32:35,680 --> 00:32:37,560
so I assume you're not
here to kidnap me again.

487
00:32:37,799 --> 00:32:39,079
If that's all, I'm going inside.

488
00:32:40,759 --> 00:32:42,729
I already told you I didn't do
it! Why won't you believe me?

489
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:46,720
Whether it was you or not,

490
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:48,120
what difference does it make?

491
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:50,278
I'm already fired anyway.

492
00:32:50,279 --> 00:32:51,200
Just drop it.

493
00:32:51,201 --> 00:32:52,521
What do you mean, "just drop it"?

494
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:54,679
We're clearing this up right now.

495
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,680
Don't you walk away!

496
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:57,919
Give me your boss's number.

497
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:58,759
I'll call him myself.

498
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,559
Man, have you looked at the time?

499
00:33:01,519 --> 00:33:03,118
Just because you don't sleep
doesn't mean nobody else does!

500
00:33:03,119 --> 00:33:04,279
I don't care what time it is!

501
00:33:04,359 --> 00:33:06,359
Nobody gets to frame me
for something I didn't do!

502
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:08,358
Won't give it to me, huh?

503
00:33:08,359 --> 00:33:08,920
Fine.

504
00:33:09,079 --> 00:33:10,079
I'll ask Mingkun.

505
00:33:11,319 --> 00:33:12,839
How can you be so selfish?

506
00:33:13,319 --> 00:33:15,239
Does the whole world
have to revolve around you?

507
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:16,575
Just because you have some stinking money,

508
00:33:16,599 --> 00:33:18,295
you think you can disrupt
everyone else's lives?

509
00:33:18,319 --> 00:33:19,960
Yeah, that's right!
I am selfish, so what?

510
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:21,640
Give me my phone!

511
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,640
No!

512
00:33:22,839 --> 00:33:23,519
Give it back!

513
00:33:23,519 --> 00:33:24,519
No!

514
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:26,616
Promise me you won't
bother anyone at this hour,

515
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,959
and I'll believe you didn't do it.

516
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:29,160
It had nothing to do with you.

517
00:33:29,759 --> 00:33:31,400
It's just my own bad luck, okay?

518
00:33:31,599 --> 00:33:32,599
I'll just suck it up.

519
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:33,720
Are you satisfied now?

520
00:33:40,759 --> 00:33:42,160
What the hell are you doing?

521
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,680
Who told you to grab my phone?

522
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,440
Fine!

523
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:47,400
Walk away, then!

524
00:33:47,401 --> 00:33:49,239
Let's see which costs more—your phone

525
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,359
or my beat-up bike!

526
00:33:51,039 --> 00:33:52,039
Bye!

527
00:34:35,085 --> 00:34:36,165
Could you please—

528
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:37,920
Keep your voice down!

529
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:39,639
This isn't your giant mansion.

530
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:41,159
Stop waking up the neighbors.

531
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,159
Did you do that on purpose?

532
00:34:56,639 --> 00:34:57,639
Ow, that hurts!

533
00:34:59,719 --> 00:35:01,879
Being this sensitive to pain
is going to be a problem.

534
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:03,880
A problem how?

535
00:35:08,639 --> 00:35:10,479
I'm saying, if you can't
handle a little pain,

536
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:12,360
what are you going to do in the future?

537
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:15,936
If you can't even handle
this little bit of pain,

538
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,520
what are you going to do in the future?

539
00:35:20,519 --> 00:35:21,736
I'm allowed to be sensitive to pain,

540
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:22,760
but you're not.

541
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:26,320
Why am I not allowed?

542
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:28,400
Are you crazy?

543
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:31,559
Not nearly as crazy as you.

544
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:36,920
Your...

545
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:39,280
That bike of yours,

546
00:35:39,320 --> 00:35:40,840
the brakes are really busted?

547
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:42,320
Mmm.

548
00:35:42,559 --> 00:35:43,000
Yeah,

549
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:43,480
they're broken.

550
00:35:43,481 --> 00:35:45,095
If they're broken, why
haven't you fixed them?

551
00:35:45,119 --> 00:35:46,799
Aren't you afraid of running someone over?

552
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:49,679
You wouldn't understand,
but for a poor guy like me,

553
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:51,639
fixing this bike costs a fortune.

554
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:53,280
Plus, I'm pretty broke lately.

555
00:35:56,639 --> 00:35:57,920
Are you trying to guilt-trip me?

556
00:35:59,119 --> 00:36:00,639
Good thing I'm blessed with good luck,

557
00:36:01,079 --> 00:36:02,839
otherwise you would've
run me over ages ago.

558
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,599
Didn't I tell you a long time ago

559
00:36:04,719 --> 00:36:06,159
to stop riding that thing?

560
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:08,000
Don't accuse me of things I didn't do!

561
00:36:08,039 --> 00:36:09,479
Oh, so you know how it
feels to be falsely accused?

562
00:36:09,480 --> 00:36:10,760
Yet you still blamed me earlier!

563
00:36:17,039 --> 00:36:18,559
Did you really not set that up?

564
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:19,880
I swear I'm gonna—.

565
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:20,880
Okay!

566
00:36:21,719 --> 00:36:23,000
Fine, I blamed you unfairly.

567
00:36:29,519 --> 00:36:31,718
Then why would my boss say that?

568
00:36:31,719 --> 00:36:34,400
That buddy of yours has a fuse
shorter than a stick of dynamite.

569
00:36:34,960 --> 00:36:37,040
How many times has he
thrown a punch at me on sight?

570
00:36:37,079 --> 00:36:38,079
If I were the boss,

571
00:36:38,119 --> 00:36:39,199
I wouldn't hire him either.

572
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:41,239
The guy's a walking time bomb.

573
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:44,558
Since you put it that way,

574
00:36:44,559 --> 00:36:45,559
you're a boss.

575
00:36:46,480 --> 00:36:47,519
Would you hire me?

576
00:36:51,559 --> 00:36:52,559
I...

577
00:36:58,320 --> 00:36:59,320
I'd...

578
00:37:05,639 --> 00:37:07,360
want you dead!

579
00:37:12,079 --> 00:37:13,079
Want me dead?

580
00:37:13,719 --> 00:37:14,880
Starting this again, are we?

581
00:37:19,119 --> 00:37:19,800
All done.

582
00:37:19,801 --> 00:37:20,919
Patched you up.

583
00:37:20,920 --> 00:37:21,920
You should head home.

584
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,000
Wait a second.

585
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,360
I...

586
00:37:27,679 --> 00:37:28,679
Sit back down first.

587
00:37:32,599 --> 00:37:33,719
What else do you want?

588
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:38,559
Look, you didn't stick this on right.

589
00:37:38,639 --> 00:37:39,919
See? It's peeling off, isn't it?

590
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:42,800
Pao Bei!

591
00:37:43,039 --> 00:37:44,039
You're back!

592
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:45,719
Why aren't you coming inside?

593
00:37:47,559 --> 00:37:48,760
I just have a few things

594
00:37:49,519 --> 00:37:50,599
to talk over with this guy.

595
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:56,400
Wait, are you...

596
00:37:56,599 --> 00:37:58,839
that big evil monster my
brother's always talking about?

597
00:37:59,760 --> 00:38:00,760
Why are you at our house?

598
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:03,376
You're not here to take
my brother away, are you?

599
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:04,400
I won't let you!

600
00:38:07,480 --> 00:38:08,598
Don't worry.

601
00:38:08,599 --> 00:38:10,079
I won't take your brother away.

602
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,480
Besides,

603
00:38:12,079 --> 00:38:14,559
is this how your brother talks
about me behind my back?

604
00:38:15,920 --> 00:38:17,639
An evil monster?

605
00:38:20,159 --> 00:38:21,360
It's okay, Xiaotong.

606
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:22,079
Don't worry.

607
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:23,416
No one is taking me anywhere.

608
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:24,440
Oh.

609
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:26,000
That's good.

610
00:38:26,119 --> 00:38:27,119
Bro,

611
00:38:27,159 --> 00:38:28,480
I'm gonna go take out the trash.

612
00:38:28,599 --> 00:38:29,599
Okay.

613
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:34,320
Does he hate me?

614
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,840
I can't believe you actually noticed.

615
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,559
My brother rarely hates anyone.

616
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:42,039
You're one of the few.

617
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:44,440
Why does he hate me?

618
00:38:44,679 --> 00:38:46,239
And why did he call me an evil monster?

619
00:38:46,599 --> 00:38:47,760
Well, he's not wrong.

620
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:49,198
You're always picking on me.

621
00:38:49,199 --> 00:38:50,776
If you're not a monster, then what are you?

622
00:38:50,800 --> 00:38:51,839
Besides,

623
00:38:51,840 --> 00:38:53,519
having people hate you,

624
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:55,960
aren't you used to that by now?

625
00:38:58,320 --> 00:38:58,760
Hey.

626
00:38:58,760 --> 00:38:59,760
Huh?

627
00:39:00,039 --> 00:39:00,639
Come here.

628
00:39:00,639 --> 00:39:01,639
Okay.

629
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:08,360
Do you hate me?

630
00:39:08,559 --> 00:39:09,559
Yeah.

631
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:13,280
If you're nicer to me,
I'll stop hating you.

632
00:39:13,519 --> 00:39:14,519
Tell me, then.

633
00:39:15,679 --> 00:39:16,879
How can I be nicer to you?

634
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:18,239
Do something that makes me happy,

635
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:20,320
and I won't hate you anymore.

636
00:39:20,599 --> 00:39:21,839
Something that makes you happy?

637
00:39:23,039 --> 00:39:24,440
What would make you happy?

638
00:39:24,679 --> 00:39:26,159
Even if I tell you, you won't do it.

639
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:27,480
I'm not telling.

640
00:39:28,159 --> 00:39:29,159
Just tell me.

641
00:39:29,519 --> 00:39:30,519
I promise I'll do it.

642
00:39:30,719 --> 00:39:31,719
I don't believe you.

643
00:39:32,599 --> 00:39:34,079
What is it with you and your brother?

644
00:39:34,199 --> 00:39:36,095
Were you two lied to your
whole lives or something?

645
00:39:36,119 --> 00:39:37,440
You don't trust anyone.

646
00:39:38,639 --> 00:39:39,959
So you're not gonna tell me, huh?

647
00:39:40,039 --> 00:39:40,519
Fine.

648
00:39:40,719 --> 00:39:41,759
I'll figure it out myself.

649
00:39:47,519 --> 00:39:48,519
A Pong,

650
00:39:49,159 --> 00:39:50,279
I need to ask you for a favor.

651
00:39:50,280 --> 00:39:51,800
Please look after Xiaotong and Xiaoya.

652
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:53,360
Just tell them

653
00:39:54,519 --> 00:39:55,960
that I took on a well-paying job

654
00:39:58,039 --> 00:40:00,079
and have to go away on
a business trip for a while.

655
00:40:00,760 --> 00:40:02,440
Tell them to be good,

656
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:05,200
and I'll take them to the
amusement park when I get back.

657
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:09,535
I'll take you guys to the amusement park.

658
00:40:09,559 --> 00:40:10,559
How does that sound?

659
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:12,159
Huh?

660
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:13,319
The amusement park?

661
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:14,360
Yeah.

662
00:40:14,840 --> 00:40:16,638
Can my sister come too?

663
00:40:16,639 --> 00:40:17,920
Of course she can.

664
00:40:18,519 --> 00:40:19,199
Big bro,

665
00:40:19,400 --> 00:40:20,519
can we go?

666
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:27,440
It just so happens.

667
00:40:27,441 --> 00:40:29,599
Milan has an event at the
amusement park tomorrow.

668
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:32,280
Invite your buddies to come along too.

669
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:36,359
I already had the organizers
get tickets for them anyway.

670
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:40,360
Consider it your Boss P'Eng being generous

671
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:43,239
and calling a truce.

672
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:44,760
What do you say?
